<section class="problem-hero"><div class="site-shell problem-hero-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">Active roof leak repair · Charlotte, NC</p><h1>Stop the water. Find the source. Repair the roof system.</h1><p>The ceiling stain is often not directly below the roof opening. Majestic traces accessible evidence, controls active entry when safe and proposes the smallest reliable repair supported by the inspection.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-gold" href="/roof-insurance-claim-charlotte-nc#claim-form">@Lang.T("Request free inspection →")</a><a class="button button-ghost" href="tel:+19808005991">@Lang.T("Call Majestic")</a></div></div><figure class="problem-hero-visual"><img src="/damage-guides/active-leak-example.webp" alt="Educational example of moisture visible on roof decking from inside an attic"/><div class="problem-icon problem-icon-leak" aria-label="DROP"><span></span><i></i><b></b></div><figcaption>@Lang.T("Educational damage example · inspection determines the actual condition")</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="problem-urgent"><div class="site-shell"><strong>@Lang.T("SAFETY FIRST")</strong><p>Keep away from wet ceilings, light fixtures and electrical equipment. Place a container only if the area is safe, move valuables and call an electrician or emergency services when electricity or ceiling collapse is a concern.</p></div></section><section class="problem-signs section"><div class="site-shell problem-clues-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("What you may notice")</p><h2>@Lang.T("Visible clues help define the inspection—not the final diagnosis.")</h2><p>@Lang.T("Use these examples to describe what you see from a safe location. A photo cannot confirm every roof layer, hidden moisture, cause or repairability.")</p></div><figure class="problem-clue-photo"><img src="/damage-guides/active-leak-example.webp" alt="Educational example of moisture visible on roof decking from inside an attic"/><figcaption>@Lang.T("Educational reference—not a Majestic customer case.")</figcaption></figure><ul><li>Dripping during or after rain</li><li>Brown ceiling rings or bubbling paint</li><li>Wet insulation or musty attic odor</li><li>Leak near a wall, valley, vent or skylight</li><li>Recurring stain after an earlier patch</li></ul></div></section><section class="problem-first section" id="first-steps"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("Before the crew arrives")</p><h2>@Lang.T("Five first steps for the homeowner.")</h2></div><p>@Lang.T("Do only what can be completed safely from the ground or a stable interior area.")</p></div><ol><li><span>01</span><p>Protect people first and avoid wet electrical areas.</p></li><li><span>02</span><p>Move belongings and document the interior location.</p></li><li><span>03</span><p>Note when the leak starts: wind-driven rain, steady rain or after the storm.</p></li><li><span>04</span><p>Do not puncture or walk under a bulging ceiling.</p></li><li><span>05</span><p>Request a roof inspection as soon as conditions permit.</p></li></ol></div></section><section class="problem-process section"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading centered-heading"><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("How Majestic handles this specific problem")</p><h2>@Lang.T("A documented path from concern to completed roof.")</h2><p>@Lang.T("The exact scope depends on safe access and what the inspection confirms. These five stages show how this particular roof condition is evaluated and repaired.")</p></div><div class="problem-process-grid"><article><span>01</span><h3>Interior reference point</h3><p>We record the stain or drip location and accessible attic evidence.</p></article><article><span>02</span><h3>Exterior tracing</h3><p>We inspect the roof path above and upslope, including valleys, flashing, shingles and penetrations.</p></article><article><span>03</span><h3>Moisture-control plan</h3><p>If safe and necessary, temporary protection is separated from the permanent repair.</p></article><article><span>04</span><h3>Repair recommendation</h3><p>We explain the observed source, affected components, proposed work and what cannot be confirmed until removal.</p></article><article><span>05</span><h3>Verification</h3><p>After authorized work, we document completion and explain what to monitor during future rain.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="arrival-section section" id="arrival"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("What happens when we arrive")</p><h2>@Lang.T("Six checkpoints from arrival through closeout.")</h2></div><p>@Lang.T("Majestic documents the roof as a construction system, explains choices before work begins and keeps insurance coverage decisions separate from contractor work.")</p></div><div class="arrival-grid"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Arrival, interview and safety check</h3><p>The technician confirms what happened, when the condition was first noticed, whether water is entering now and which interior rooms are affected. Before using a ladder, Majestic checks weather, electrical, tree, structural and fall hazards and explains any access limitation.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Interior and ground-level reference</h3><p>When relevant and accessible, the team starts at the stain, drip or impacted room, reviews the attic from a safe access point and then walks the exterior perimeter. This creates a reference line between the interior evidence and the roof area above it.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Roof-system inspection</h3><p>When safe access is available, Majestic reviews affected slopes plus shingles, ridge and hip caps, valleys, flashing, pipe boots, vents, skylights, roof edges, gutters, fascia and soffit. Wide photographs show location; detail photographs show the condition.</p></div></article><article><span>04</span><div><h3>Measurements and factual documentation</h3><p>The record identifies visible conditions, roof geometry, affected components and estimated quantities. Storm-related observations are separated from age, maintenance, installation details and hidden conditions that cannot be confirmed without authorized removal.</p></div></article><article><span>05</span><div><h3>Options explained before authorization</h3><p>Majestic explains immediate protection, localized repair, section rebuild and replacement paths when applicable. The homeowner receives a written roofing path and can choose an out-of-pocket project or use the factual documents in a claim they manage with their carrier.</p></div></article><article><span>06</span><div><h3>Construction, verification and closeout</h3><p>After a written scope is approved, materials and schedule are confirmed. Majestic performs the authorized roofing work, controls debris and cleanup, photographs completion and provides the applicable invoice, warranty and project-closeout documents.</p></div></article></div></div></section><section class="problem-repairs section" id="repairs"><div class="site-shell"><div class="section-heading split-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("Repair options")</p><h2>@Lang.T("The inspection determines which option can be built reliably.")</h2></div><p>@Lang.T("Final materials, quantities, code requirements and hidden conditions are confirmed in the written scope.")</p></div><div class="problem-repair-grid"><article><h3>Shingle repair</h3><p>Replace torn, missing or failed shingles and restore adjacent water-shedding details when the surrounding roof remains serviceable.</p></article><article><h3>Flashing or penetration repair</h3><p>Replace or rebuild failed flashing, boots, vents or related underlayment instead of relying only on surface sealant.</p></article><article><h3>Valley or transition repair</h3><p>Open the affected transition, inspect the substrate and rebuild the layered drainage path.</p></article><article><h3>Replacement</h3><p>Consider a larger replacement when multiple leaks, brittle materials, widespread failure or incompatible old repairs prevent a dependable localized solution.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="problem-source"><div class="site-shell"><span>i</span><p>GAF identifies aged shingles and deteriorated flashing around chimneys, vents and skylights as common leak sources. <a href="https://www.gaf.com/en-us/plan-design/homeowner-education/roof-damage/roof-leak-repair" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Read the source ↗</a></p></div></section><section class="faq-section section"><div class="site-shell faq-layout"><div><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("FAQ")</p><h2>@Lang.T("Clear expectations before work begins.")</h2></div><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>@Lang.T("Is the inspection free?")<span>+</span></summary><p>@Lang.T("Yes. Majestic provides a free roof inspection, photographs, a report, estimated measurements and a written project path, subject to safe access.")</p></details><details><summary>@Lang.T("Does the inspection guarantee insurance coverage?")<span>+</span></summary><p>@Lang.T("No. Majestic documents roofing conditions and scope. The carrier independently decides coverage and payment.")</p></details><details><summary>@Lang.T("Can I pay out of pocket?")<span>+</span></summary><p>@Lang.T("Yes. Majestic can explain an out-of-pocket repair or replacement path as well as the construction documentation used for a claim-related project.")</p></details><details><summary>@Lang.T("How far do you travel?")<span>+</span></summary><p>@Lang.T("Roof inspections are available approximately 90 minutes from Charlotte or Rock Hill, subject to address and schedule confirmation. Raleigh is not in the service area.")</p></details></div></div></section><section class="resource-cta section"><div class="site-shell"><p class="eyebrow">@Lang.T("Free inspection")</p><h2>@Lang.T("Photos, report, estimated measurements and a written project path.")</h2><a class="button button-gold" href="/roof-insurance-claim-charlotte-nc#claim-form">@Lang.T("Start my request →")</a></div></section>
